It's just it's really surprising to me that married women have just been perceived in that light. For me

00:16:56.520 --> 00:17:02.400
Although it's my reality as far as taking care of my child. I try not to think in a "woe is me"

00:17:03.220 --> 00:17:07.529
Situation because that's how they approach it. Just because I say, yes. It's an immediate

00:17:08.199 --> 00:17:11.189
Assumption that I'm just a single woman that can't take care of my child

00:17:11.520 --> 00:17:16.619
I just find it great to know that most of you are married as black women because I've been around single moms and

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:21.089
this kind of helped me step out of my comfort zone to know that our black community

00:17:21.089 --> 00:17:25.439
We do have households that have men in them that are care of their kids

00:17:25.949 --> 00:17:28.289
So it this is really, it's really nice

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:32.579
That's a wrap. Thank you so much

